+## Context
+
+New project with no source yet. TypeScript strict, NodeNext ESM, Node standard library only, tests with
+`node --test`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** a small in-memory service implementing the rules in the spec.
+**Non-Goals:** cancellation, persistence, season enforcement, equipment listing.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Single file `src/index.ts` exporting `createRentalService()` and the types; state lives in closure maps.
+- Periods are validated with a strict regex for `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00(.000)?Z` plus a round-trip check through
+  `Date`, so offsets, non-midnight times and impossible dates are rejected. Returned `start`/`end` are the
+  normalized `toISOString()` form.
+- Days = (end − start) / 86 400 000; this is exact because UTC has no daylight saving. Total = dailyPrice × days,
+  an integer because dailyPrice is validated as a non-negative safe integer.
+- Overlap test on half-open intervals: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`.
+- Booking ids come from `crypto.randomUUID()` (Node standard library).
+- Cancellation policy is recorded in the spec only; no code until a cancel operation is requested.
+- Assumption: bookings outside April to October are not rejected, since the rules given do not say so.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- In-memory state is lost on restart; accepted for the "basics" stage.
