+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The booking desk has no way to rent out the school's boards and sails. Desk staff need to price and book
+equipment for students and visitors, and to be sure the same item is never rented twice at the same time.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add an in-memory rental service, created with `createRentalService()` and exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` registers a board or a sail with a daily price in euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns the total price of a rental period.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` books the item for the period and returns the booking with an id.
+- Both throw for unknown items and disallowed periods; `book` also throws when the item is already booked
+  for any part of the period.
+- The school's rules (integer cents, UTC ISO-8601 times, whole days, no overlapping bookings,
+  cancellation policy) are written down in the spec.
+
+Scope: rentals of boards and sails at the booking desk.
+Out of scope: cancellations and refunds (only the policy is recorded for later), lessons, customers,
+persistence, listing or searching equipment, season (April to October) enforcement.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `rentals`: equipment registration, pricing and booking of boards and sails by whole days.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+New file `src/index.ts` (plus a test). No existing code, API or dependency is affected.
